@@ -0,0 +1,100 @@
+---
+status: accepted
+applies_to: [traceability]
+rule: Traceability warns on osq's own traceability capability until its trial decides to block, widen, or drop it.
+checks: [tests/trace-own-config.test.ts]
+---
+# 011. Traceability trial
+
+Date: 2026-10-06
+
+## Status
+
+Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+ADR 006 decision 4 says a gate either stops the flow or is removed, and a
+warning is allowed only while its signal is being measured. Traceability and
+mutation checks have shipped, but until now no capability has been opted in, so
+neither warning has produced a signal and neither can be judged. Change 154 is
+the first opt-in.
+
+It opts in `traceability` alone, because it is the smallest capability: 36
+untested scenarios and 16 unclaimed functions across 8 files. Version-control,
+where the 149 bug lived, is the next candidate at 98 scenarios and 58 functions
+in 20 files, so it would take several changes before its trial even started.
+Measuring the smallest capability first keeps the window short and the cost
+bounded.
+
+The validator (ADR 010) does not read traceability results. It judges a
+change's code against its delta scenarios, and its findings are a separate
+signal with its own measurement. Nothing here feeds it.
+
+## Decision
+
+osq opts `traceability` in under `warn` mode with focused tests and StrykerJS
+10 mutation checks, run through `tsx` under a 300-second budget per task. All
+three are observe-only: a finding or a mutation result never blocks a change,
+changes a task's done state, or triggers a retry.
+
+A **trial change** is a change whose approval prints a traceability lint
+finding, or whose task streams hold a `focused_ran` or `mutation_ran` event.
+For each trial change osq records four signals:
+
+1. **Link findings.** Every finding of the traceability lint, with each
+   unreadable form counted among them.
+2. **Mutation picks.** Each pick by outcome and, when it was not measured, its
+   reason.
+3. **Survivors.** Each surviving mutant a measured pick reports.
+4. **Time added per task.** The sum of that task's `focused_ran` and
+   `mutation_ran` durations.
+
+## Measurement
+
+The decision is due after 8 trial changes, or on 2026-12-15, whichever comes
+first. In the brief that follows, a human labels each link finding true (a real
+missing or stale link) or false, and each survivor true (a missing assertion)
+or false (noise).
+
+- **Block.** `traceability` moves to `require` mode when at least three
+  quarters of the link findings are true, at least three quarters of the picks
+  are measured, and the median time added per task with a pick is at most
+  120 s.
+- **Widen.** `version-control` is opted in, still in `warn` mode, for one more
+  window of the same size, when the block thresholds hold but the window holds
+  fewer than 10 link findings and picks in all.
+- **Drop.** The opt-in and the mutation command are removed when fewer than
+  half the link findings are true, fewer than half the picks are measured, or
+  the median time added per task is over 300 s.
+- **Anything else.** One more window of the same size, and then traceability
+  must block or go.
+- **Mutation checks** stay only if at least one in four labeled survivors is
+  true. Otherwise the command is dropped, whatever the link decision.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Most mutation picks cost about 5 s, but a pick of `scenario` costs about
+  171 s. A task that changes the helper and another tagged function can
+  therefore spend more than half the 300-second budget on one pick and record
+  `budget` for a third.
+- Twelve prose mentions of `@scenario` in `src/` are already reported
+  unreadable, so lint warns about them whenever a change scopes one of those
+  files. They are false positives, and this trial counts them as such.
+- `scanSource`'s picks are `range_unknown`, because its helpers hold regular
+  expression literals whose brackets osq's range counter cannot balance. Every
+  pick of it is a not-measured pick until that is fixed.
+- Until the measurement says otherwise, the opt-in, the focused run, and the
+  mutation checks are all advice a human reads, not gates.
+
+## Rejected
+
+- **Opting in every capability at once.** Version-control alone spans 20 files
+  and nearly three times the scenarios, so the window would start late and the
+  cost would hide in the noise.
+- **A homegrown mutator.** The trial measures what osq tells projects to run.
+  StrykerJS is the README's reference setup and a dev dependency, so the
+  runtime dependency rule needs no ADR.
+- **Starting in `require` mode.** Traceability has never run against a real
+  capability. Its false-positive rate is unknown, and ADR 006 decision 4 does
+  not allow a warning to block before its signal has been measured.
